  "title": "Rubric Dropout",
  "summary": "This paper introduces a method to mitigate reward hacking in Rubric-Based Reinforcement Learning (RL) by randomly dropping a subset of criteria before computing the reward. The proposed approach uses Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) to ensure that policy models never optimize the same rubric twice, thereby preventing reward hacking and improving the quality and security of training.",
